(LOG: EXECUTIVE FINDINGS \(CoEES / OIL R&D\): Statistical analysis of 24 directional) Tj T*
(wells in Block NHR-04 and NHR-05 reveals a 68% incidence of severe lost) Tj T*
(circulation \(10–22 bbl/hr\) and subsequent coal-packoff stuck pipe within a narrow) Tj T*
(50-meter depth window \(3,400 m to 3,450 m MD\) inside the middle Barail Coal-Shale) Tj T*
(member. Because Barail coal cleats possess aperture widths of 80–220 microns,) Tj T*
(conventional bentonite mud fails to bridge until massive losses occur. Proactive) Tj T*
(wellbore strengthening \('Stress Caging'\) must be initiated 15 to 25 meters ABOVE) Tj T*
(the 3,400 m top—specifically at 3,380–3,390 m—by staging a 25 bbl bimodal LCM pill) Tj T*
